    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 6,
        "sourceEnd": 241,
        "text": "Okay, everyone, thanks for coming. This is the final planning meeting for the Riverfront Innovation Hub. We have forty minutes. Let's start with the budget. The city has promised two million dollars, but we still need private partners.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "22fbe827b3b7f0c5349e04e6c658e0ce283cde4ce26aa4e1d29363930158ad58",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 251,
        "sourceEnd": 443,
        "text": "Right. I've spoken to three tech companies. Two are interested, but they want their names on the main building. I think that's a problem. The hub should be for everyone, not just for sponsors.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "a514324b09d5701f7c88ca2fc737707a8bd7106fece61ab42a8ac17060190de0",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 452,
        "sourceEnd": 638,
        "text": "I agree with the principle, Daniel, but we can't ignore the money. Without private partners, we can't open next spring. Maybe we can offer smaller signs inside, not on the main building.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "39418505951bfa83ebe28874f59e262c41675869fe4dcb760f90360fb075dce9",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 648,
        "sourceEnd": 783,
        "text": "That could work. But I still think we should limit how much influence companies have. They shouldn't decide which projects get funding.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "00c4d7937e8e17c2089cfb85e6b85baa7071fef5461523c1ca8a6df25626c77a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 791,
        "sourceEnd": 932,
        "text": "Good point. Let's separate money from decisions. Companies can give money, but the community board decides the projects. Does everyone agree?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "b8f7eec51a76d7242de7f6fc81099c0f438e6bd60a0e6de1288bd9fbde17268d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 941,
        "sourceEnd": 1113,
        "text": "Mostly, yes. Though I'd add one thing: the companies might not give money if they have no voice at all. We could give them one seat on the board, but not a vote on funding.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "cf931e3b7cb44aba12d0b93a2c24cbb0b2f038540162b67881aea9828c25017e",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 1123,
        "sourceEnd": 1242,
        "text": "Hmm. I'm not sure about that. A seat without a vote seems strange. But I can accept it if the community has more seats.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "c51cf232ccd4677253e997620dcabf8636c43be3743da266907e6e6a433b469a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1250,
        "sourceEnd": 1424,
        "text": "Okay, let's say the board has nine members: five from the community, two from the city, and two from private partners. And only the community members vote on project funding.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "313a8cb5c08ff8e8cf5fc8b759a91c9127671ee6e8af98cc5fb39a949a01f3e8",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 1433,
        "sourceEnd": 1512,
        "text": "Sorry, Maya, did you say two from private partners? I thought we agreed on one.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "b34a91cff002755a48303092be9b3382e1086fdaee620148438d2ce406e0a086",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1520,
        "sourceEnd": 1698,
        "text": "You're right, I misspoke. One from private partners. So the board is eight members: five community, two city, one private partner. And the private partner has no vote on funding.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "c3e680fa48fc2f9056ef48d19d7d245cffeafd7eebfba639cf489637e83afdc4",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 1708,
        "sourceEnd": 1844,
        "text": "That sounds fair. Now, what about the training programs? I want to make sure local residents get the jobs, not just people from outside.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "30224372bdb7a28159c7dd8c454cdd448b3aa960412f2a158f245bcca325082c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 1853,
        "sourceEnd": 1990,
        "text": "I agree. We should require that at least sixty percent of the construction jobs go to people who live within five kilometers of the site.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "5eb128a59c15b9493e85e2c13598cae8623c5e8fa7e952b96cce021445a956c5",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 2000,
        "sourceEnd": 2115,
        "text": "Sixty percent? That's high. Can local workers fill that many jobs? I'm worried we won't find enough skilled people.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "609596868df39075696e637a6b7e12805f45d09164f8bd65a6a3c835c8a0dd6d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 2124,
        "sourceEnd": 2302,
        "text": "That's why we need the training program first. We can train local people in basic construction skills before the main building work starts. The training can run for three months.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "d298910c226a5285f1830770651f281de237574231b889f8b628f54bdb790c02",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2310,
        "sourceEnd": 2408,
        "text": "I like that. But who pays for the training? The city budget is for the building, not for training.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "34ab2650dc300b779bfdddca69a7a2b269e589489065c6e42048d7c826b64c68",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 2418,
        "sourceEnd": 2566,
        "text": "The private partner could pay for training. That would be a good use of their money, and it would help them too, because they'd get skilled workers.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "f73bea5de44f8f723a01d5d94438962c6776773c983a90a2890cb9e480f2d621",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 2575,
        "sourceEnd": 2698,
        "text": "True, but I'm not convinced they'll agree. They want to see a return. Training doesn't look like a return on a spreadsheet.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "849c12d877199ab2951dff5b9448c51108357f218dfb098a7d881c63c09a59e9",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2706,
        "sourceEnd": 2826,
        "text": "Maybe we can show them that trained local workers are cheaper than bringing people from far away. That's a real benefit.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "6d4298a165d47d8b28a151fb7af12a3755c290d733494159ef2e01de81bf8da1",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 2836,
        "sourceEnd": 3009,
        "text": "I think we should ask them. If they say no, we can look for a government training grant. There's a program called Skills Now that gives money for exactly this kind of thing.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "73523028ea230e9b0ca90ea8b72d258ef83cb67d9f22122a1ed763249d897d4d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 3018,
        "sourceEnd": 3165,
        "text": "Okay, I'll contact them. But I want to be clear: if the private partner pays for training, they still don't get a vote on funding. That's separate.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "26309b4d399b596fd61ef4879d7d2f016b8e3ac494e0f538bee4dab53e8fdc18",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 3173,
        "sourceEnd": 3327,
        "text": "Agreed. Now, the last thing: the public space. The original plan had a small park on the north side. But the revised plan has a parking lot there instead.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "612248017fb62c6dab804755f8b77c2f3cabdf46713ca1ccc972937bc6e19d09",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 3337,
        "sourceEnd": 3372,
        "text": "I didn't know that. Who changed it?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "02e0a2c5b1a37d95e34876ab7da165a708c82d7ef7b30ad687111933f71bd344",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 3380,
        "sourceEnd": 3519,
        "text": "The city changed it last month. They said the parking lot is needed for the hub's visitors. But I think a park is better for the community.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "f956395b6292247c58453f41c7983f5d3a96890a1d4ee6b1a5a60cd7c5c764c7",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 3528,
        "sourceEnd": 3670,
        "text": "I agree with Maya. A park brings people together. A parking lot doesn't. But we have to be realistic: without parking, some people won't come.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "dbb26937bdd0e776cca81ed11ef02189ddbbe2e1fd605348209aa9c35e8301b1",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 3680,
        "sourceEnd": 3741,
        "text": "Could we have both? A smaller parking lot and a smaller park?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "bc5d5f66daadfb2724e5df9b4af8cacbe912b9c3c9c0b48c1aa2e47d0906e03a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 3749,
        "sourceEnd": 3880,
        "text": "That's possible. The city might accept a compromise. Let's propose a parking lot for thirty cars and a park on the remaining space.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "77c6a6882b7fd128615f97e7e30bf3d179ccce02b28ac4cddac156b8df719744",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 3889,
        "sourceEnd": 4002,
        "text": "I can support that. Though I still think the park should be bigger. But compromise is better than no park at all.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "098a7b3d2d1819aeb2f32c46900642a18e09a560a150265634aa72307b119658",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 4012,
        "sourceEnd": 4252,
        "text": "Fine. So, to summarize: eight board members, one private partner without a funding vote, sixty percent local construction jobs, training paid by the private partner if possible, and a compromise on the park and parking. Did I miss anything?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "a851ebe19bf70a5bbb6decbf2576d4391166be7d0289c28fe3283a7570d08838",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 4260,
        "sourceEnd": 4315,
        "text": "No, that's everything. I'll send the notes to everyone.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "be88bb98f96be2541707bc6dcc5f1d5bf2fdbfa5b66b0c675fbd28689deea279",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.7
      }
    ]
  },
